From 1b0fcc86595d7aeb8d53d64467cbd4204528fa21 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Lane A <lane-a@local.invalid>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 21:59:26 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 06/22] feat(layout): "face on top, game below" templates for
 streamer clips

Luffy's reference reel (gaming pages' streamer cuts): the facecam,
cropped tight, fills the top 45 % of the frame, the gameplay fills the
bottom, a coloured divider marks the seam, captions sit centred on the
seam one to three words at a time, and a small credit line sits at the
bottom. Two looks: facecam_red (red divider, white Anton with a red
outline) and facecam_gold (gold divider, white with a black outline,
spoken word in yellow).

- media/gaming_templates.py builds the graph; choose_reaction_layout
  uses it when the task picked a template and a facecam is found.
- Per-task layout_template / layout_credit: migration
  20261117_0001, model, repository, POST /tasks/ (422 on a bad
  template), processing and every clip re-render path. NULL keeps the
  automatic layout; the render call shape is unchanged without it.
- Caption templates seam_red / seam_gold; the template's caption look
  wins over the task font and the profile's words-per-line.
- Create form: a "Gaming layout" picker (Gaming niche only) and a
  credit box, 6 locales, 4 vitest tests; tsc clean.
- The credit drawtext reads a temp file (user text never enters the
  graph); its cleanup timer is a daemon so short-lived processes exit.
- Four hand-written SQLite mirrors of the tasks table gain the two
  columns, as they did for framing_mode.
- Phase 2 harness: --layout-template / --credit / --out-suffix, and
  --only runs merge into INDEX.md.

Proof: Kai Cenat 1080p, both templates, 4/4 clips rendered with seam
captions and credit; 14 backend tests, 4 frontend tests.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
